invariant: INV-26
file: gcm_avx512_kernel.c
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: gcm_avx512_kernel.c drops the target attribute that turns VAES,
  VPCLMULQDQ, AVX-512F and AVX-512BW on for its own functions, so the
  kernel compiles only where the whole object is built with those
  instructions, and an object built that way runs AVX-512 in code the
  caller's ch_cfg.cpu never chose. The script compiles the file for x86-64
  with no instruction flag, as a host object compiles it, and the compile
  fails: each intrinsic needs a feature only the attribute turned on.

--- old
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(                                                                      \
    __attribute__((target("aes,pclmul,avx2,avx512f,avx512bw,vaes,vpclmulqdq"))),                   \
    apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#pragma GCC target("aes,pclmul,avx2,avx512f,avx512bw,vaes,vpclmulqdq")
#endif
--- new
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((cold)), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#endif
